{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26342 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (3S,7S,8S,9S,10R,13R,14S,17R)-17-[(2R,5R)-5-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-6-methylheptan-2-yl]-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-dodecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthrene-3,7-diol and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that interact with this complex. These compounds include 6-Methoxykaempferol-3-O-Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, [3-(3-Hydroxy-4,5-dimethoxyphenyl)-3-oxopropyl] acetate, and (Z)-Calacorene. The shared target of these compounds indicates that the compound may be involved in pathways where EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex plays a role, possibly in gene regulation or epigenetic processes. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a possible mechanism where the compound interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a common target, the macrophage scavenger receptor types I and II. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are similar across the different paths, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains uncertain.",
